Subject: [RFC PATCH 0/2] Input: add Lenovo TB710FU Keyboard Pack driver

This series adds a driver for the detachable Keyboard Pack of the Lenovo
TB710FU tablet (Xiaoxin Pad Pro GT, SM8650). The keyboard, its touchpad
and the fold state share a 921600 baud UART on the pogo pins.

The TB710FU board is not in mainline yet, so this series has no in-tree
user. The board devicetree will be sent separately.

I am sending this as an RFC because I would like your opinion on three
design points:

1. Plug detection. The detect line is a GPIO that the board describes as
   a gpio-keys SW_DOCK switch, and the driver follows that switch with an
   input handler. The alternative is a detect-gpios property, with the
   driver owning the GPIO and reporting SW_DOCK itself. Which do you
   prefer?

2. Location. The reports look like HID reports after descrambling. Would
   you prefer a HID transport driver over a plain input driver in
   drivers/input/keyboard?

3. Device lifetime. The input devices are registered when a keyboard is
   attached and removed when it is detached, so that desktops can tell
   whether a physical keyboard is present.

The protocol and the scrambling table were obtained by disassembling the
vendor kernel module (lenovo_keyboard.ko) and observing the UART traffic.
No vendor source code is included.

Known limitations:

- The touchpad resolution is an estimate from the size of the pad.
- The meaning of consumer usages 0x394 and 0x395 is not known. They are
  mapped to KEY_FULL_SCREEN and KEY_PROG2.
- The Caps Lock LED is dimmer than under the vendor firmware. The cause
  is not known.

Testing:

- An earlier revision of this driver is in daily use on a TB710FU with a
  7.2.6-based kernel: typing, touchpad, Caps Lock LED, attach and detach,
  folding the keyboard back, and suspend to idle.
- This revision was cleaned up for submission. It builds against v7.4-rc3
  with W=1, and the binding passes dt_binding_check.
